        "problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
